# Synthesizer UI (XP60Studio)

Full rules: `docs/design/SYNTHESIZER_UI_AGENT_GUIDELINES.md`.

## Non-negotiable for Design / Play musical surfaces

- Do **not** default to `ParameterValueEditor`, `XpSpinField`, `TextField`, or `ComboBox` as the primary control for continuous or musically meaningful params.
- Prefer `MusicalParamKnob` / `XpKnob`, `EnvelopeEditor`, `KeyboardStrip`, `XpRangeBar`, choice chips, `TonePlaySettingsStrip`, Effects nodes.
- Exact entry is secondary (readout toggle / Exact disclosure). Keep `objectName`s for tests.
- Do not invent XP-60 envelope curves, wavetable morphs, or MIDI-CC learn menus the product does not support yet.
- Reuse Theme / catalog components; match `xp60studio-ui-master-mockup.jpg` composition.

## Allowed primary text/spin

Search, patch name, paths, device/port IDs, Expert raw grids, diagnostics.

## Before finishing UI work

Screenshot with `xp60studio_screenshot`, run relevant `tst_qml`, and note remaining Directive Alpha violations in the UI report if any.
